vidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"urolithiasis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.93,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"dsc:2.130":{"ref":"De materia medica 2.130","headword":"κορωνόποὗς πρόμηκές ἐστι","lang":"grc","source":"dioscorides","text":"κορωνόποὗς πρόμηκές ἐστι βοτάνιον, κατὰ τοῦ ἐδάφους κατεστρωμένον, κατεσχισμένον τὰ φύλλα· λαχανεύεται δὲ καὶ τοῦτο ἑφθόν. τούτου ποιεῖ ἡ ῥίζα πρὸς κοιλιακοὺς ἐσθιομένη.","spans":[{"start":148,"end":155,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"therapeutic"}]},"cul:051-bucks-horn-plantain":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Buck’s-Horn Plantain","headword":"Buck’s-Horn Plantain","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"It is under the dominion of Saturn, and is of a gallant, drying, and binding quality. This boiled in wine and drank, and some of the leaves put to the hurt place, is an excellent remedy for the biting of the viper or adder, which I take to be one and the same. The same being also drank, helps those that are troubled with the stone in the reins or kidneys, by cooling the heat of the part afflicted, and strengthens them; also weak stomachs that cannot retain, but cast up their meat. It stays all bleeding both at mouth or nose; bloody urine or the bloody-flux, and stops the lask of the belly and bowels. The leaves hereof bruised and laid to their sides that have an ague, suddenly ease the fits; and the leaves and roots applied to the wrists, works the same effect. The herb boiled in ale and wine, and given for some mornings and evenings together, stays the distillation of hot and sharp rheums falling into the eyes from the head, and helps all sorts of sore eyes.","spans":[{"start":194,"end":203,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":208,"end":213,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":217,"end":222,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":327,"end":332,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":340,"end":345,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":349,"end":356,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":428,"end":441,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":499,"end":529,"concept_id":"nosebleed","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":531,"end":543,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":551,"end":562,"concept_id":"dysentery","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":578,"end":582,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":671,"end":675,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":866,"end":878,"concept_id":"common_cold","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":896,"end":924,"concept_id":"conjunctivitis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":963,"end":972,"concept_id":"conjunctivitis","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"dsc:2.130":{"148":"coeliac affection (κοιλιακοί)"},"cul:051-bucks-horn-plantain":{"194":"biting / stinging of (serpents, scorpions, beasts)","208":"serpents, vipers, adders, scorpions, wasps","217":"serpents, vipers, adders, scorpions, wasps","327":"the stone (urinary calculus)","340":"reins: kidneys","349":"kidneys","428":"weak / cold / hot stomach (dyspepsia)","499":"bleeding at the nose (and mouth)","531":"bloody urine: haematuria","551":"bloody flux: dysentery","578":"lask: diarrhoea, looseness of the bowels","671":"agues: intermittent fevers","866":"distillation / defluxion of rheum from the head: catarrh","896":"defluxion of rheum into the eyes","963":"sore eyes"}},"images":[]}